<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Finding coefficients from a stationary point</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The curve \(y = x^3 + ax^2 + bx + 4\) has a stationary point at \(({@p0@}, {@kk@})\).</p><p>(a) Find \(a\) and \(b\).</p><div>\(a =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] \(\quad b =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) The stationary point is a [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Two facts give two equations. The gradient is \(0\) at the point, and the point lies on the curve.</p><p>\(\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 + 2ax + b\). At \(x = {@p0@}\): \({@3*p0^2+2*p0*a+b@} = 0\).</p><p>The curve passes through \(({@p0@}, {@kk@})\): \({@p0^3+p0^2*a+p0*b+4@} = {@kk@}\).</p><p>Solving these simultaneously gives \(a = {@a0@}\) and \(b = {@b0@}\), so \(y = {@f@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\dfrac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 6x + 2a = {@6*x+2*a0@}\), which is \({@f2@}\) at \(x = {@p0@}\): [[if test="is(f2>0)"]]positive[[else]]negative[[/if]], so the point is a [[if test="is(np=1)"]]maximum point[[elif test="is(np=2)"]]minimum point[[else]]point of inflection[[/if]].</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: a stationary point fixes two constants, with diagnostics for using only one of the two facts. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 1, chapter 9, Mixed questions question 10. */
L: [[1,-5],[2,-4],[-1,1],[3,-3],[-2,-1],[1,3],[2,-9],[-1,-6],[-3,3],[2,1]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
p0: L[ix][1]; a0: L[ix][2];
b0: -3*p0^2-2*a0*p0;
kk: p0^3+a0*p0^2+b0*p0+4;
f2: 6*p0+2*a0;
np: if f2<0 then 1 else 2;
f: x^3+a0*x^2+b0*x+4;
nat2: [["max2",is(np=1),"maximum point"],["min2",is(np=2),"minimum point"],["inf2",is(np=3),"point of inflection"]];
wa2: if np=1 then "min2" else "max2";
wb2: if np=3 then "min2" else "inf2";
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
