  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Differentiation II: finding coefficients from a stationary point</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 4.1: Use the two facts at a given stationary point to find two coefficients of a cubic, then classify the point.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 10 in the Mixed questions of Chapter 9 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 1 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: two unknown constants instead of one, randomised over curated points, with diagnostics for using only one fact.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
